/-!
# Arithmetic generated by one minimal source

The arithmetic component of
`GeneratedFoundations.CommonFoundation.fromMinimalUnbiasedChange` takes only a
minimal unbiased compositional change datum. Its conclusion covers every
carrier orientation and positive width; these index realizations of the same construction. The
coordinate is the trace pairing with the oriented unit. The two Gaussian
densities, correlation endpoints, original Neumann domain and lifted original
endomorphisms are constructed from that source at the same width.

The calibrated information and peak-equivalent width are internal readout
definitions. Reflection constructs the finite-window operator, and the
separated boundary comparison proves its uniqueness within the stated class.
No endpoint or boundary operator is supplied by the caller, and these
comparison conclusions do not assert uniqueness among arbitrary readout or
closure rules. No absolute width is selected. The native
operations are modulation and composition on the original maps; winding
provides their numerical certificate after those operations are defined.
Unique factorization is inherited from the internal Euclidean construction,
not from a factorization theorem on the certificate values.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

